Dialogue: 0,00:01:07.73,00:01:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Thebes, City of the Living,
Dialogue: 0,00:01:11.15,00:01:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,crown Jewel of Pharaoh \NSETI the First.
Dialogue: 0,00:01:16.99,00:01:21.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Home of Imhotep, \NPharaoh's high priest,
Dialogue: 0,00:01:21.50,00:01:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,keeper of the dead.
Dialogue: 0,00:01:25.33,00:01:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Birthplace of Anck-Su-Namun, \NPharaoh's mistress.
Dialogue: 0,00:01:28.80,00:01:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No other man was allowed \Nto touch her...
Dialogue: 0,00:01:54.53,00:01:58.53,Default,,0,0,0,,But for their love, they were \Nwilling to risk life itself.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:47.81,00:03:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,To resurrect Anck-Su-Namun,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:49.81,00:03:53.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep and his priests broke into \Nher crypt and stole her body.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:54.73,00:03:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,They raced deep into the desert,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:56.53,00:03:59.32,Default,,0,0,0,,taking Anck-Su-Namun's corpse to \NHamunaptra, City of the Dead,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:59.40,00:04:00.66,Default,,0,0,0,,HAMUNAPTRA - 1290 B.C.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:00.74,00:04:03.70,Default,,0,0,0,,ancient burial site for \Nthe sons of pharaohs
Dialogue: 0,00:04:03.87,00:04:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,and resting place for \Nthe wealth of Egypt.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:09.83,00:04:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,For his love, Imhotep dared the gods' \Nanger by going deep into the city,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:15.21,00:04:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,where he took the black Book of the \NDead from it's holy resting place.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:20.68,00:04:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Anck-Su-Namun's soul had been \Nsent to the dark underworld,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:24.68,00:04:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,her vital organs removed and placed \Nin five sacred Canopic jars.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:59.17,00:05:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Anck-Su-Namun's soul had \Ncome back from the dead,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:03.39,00:05:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,but Pharaoh's bodyguards had \Nfollowed lmhotep and stopped him
Dialogue: 0,00:05:06.76,00:05:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,before the ritual \Ncould be completed.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:24.45,00:05:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He was to remain sealed \Ninside his sarcophagus,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:27.91,00:05:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,be undead for all of eternity.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:30.83,00:05:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The Magi would never allow \Nhim to be released,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:33.87,00:05:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,for he would arise a walking \Ndisease, a plague upon mankind,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:38.09,00:05:41.34,Default,,0,0,0,,an unholy flesh-eater with \Nthe strength of ages,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:41.55,00:05:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,power over the sands, and \Nthe Glory of invincibility.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:18.42,00:06:22.51,Default,,0,0,0,,For 3,000 years, men and \Narmies fought over this land,
Dialogue: 0,00:06:22.63,00:06:25.09,Default,,0,0,0,,never knowing what \Nevil lay beneath it.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:41.98,00:06:45.07,Default,,0,0,0,,And for 3,000 years, \Nwe, the Magi,
Dialogue: 0,00:06:45.15,00:06:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,the descendants of Pharaoh's \Nsacred bodyguards, kept watch.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:03.05,00:07:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You just got promoted.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:12.14,00:07:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Steady!
Dialogue: 0,00:07:13.85,00:07:17.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're with me on this one, right? \N- Your strength gives me strength.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:19.65,00:07:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Steady!
Dialogue: 0,00:07:24.73,00:07:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait! Wait for me!
Dialogue: 0,00:07:28.36,00:07:29.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Steady!
Dialogue: 0,00:07:34.100,00:07:36.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,00:09:01.87,00:09:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Run, Beni! Run!
Dialogue: 0,00:09:03.92,00:09:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Get inside! Get inside!
Dialogue: 0,00:09:08.51,00:09:11.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! Don't you close that door!
Dialogue: 0,00:09:11.26,00:09:13.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you close that door!
Dialogue: 0,00:10:13.11,00:10:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You will die. You will die.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:16.72,00:11:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,CAIRO, EGYPT - 3 YEARS LATER
Dialogue: 0,00:11:31.65,00:11:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Sacred stones,
Dialogue: 0,00:11:34.28,00:11:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,sculpture and aesthetics,
Dialogue: 0,00:11:37.95,00:11:42.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Socrates, Seth, volume \None, volume two,
Dialogue: 0,00:11:43.08,00:11:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,and volume three.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:45.50,00:11:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,00:11:47.96,00:11:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Tuthmosis. What are \Nyou doing here?
Dialogue: 0,00:11:52.25,00:11:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,T. T, t, t...
Dialogue: 0,00:11:54.25,00:11:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,T.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:56.92,00:11:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to put you \Nwhere you belong!
Dialogue: 0,00:12:16.90,00:12:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Help.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:46.43,00:12:47.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Oops.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:47.64,00:12:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What... How...
Dialogue: 0,00:12:56.02,00:12:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, look at this!
Dialogue: 0,00:12:58.74,00:13:00.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Sons of the pharaohs!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:01.11,00:13:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me frogs! Flies! Locusts!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:05.16,00:13:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Anything but you!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:07.83,00:13:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Compared to you, the other \Nplagues were a Joy!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:10.66,00:13:13.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I am so very sorry. \NIt was an accident.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:13.46,00:13:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,My girl, when Rameses destroyed \NSyria, that was an accident.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:18.13,00:13:20.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You are a catastrophe!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:20.88,00:13:22.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at my library!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:22.84,00:13:24.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Why do I put up with you?
Dialogue: 0,00:13:25.60,00:13:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you put up with \Nme because I can...
Dialogue: 0,00:13:28.52,00:13:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I can read and write \NAncient Egyptian,
Dialogue: 0,00:13:31.68,00:13:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,and I can... I can decipher \Nhieroglyphics and hieratic,
Dialogue: 0,00:13:35.19,00:13:38.73,Default,,0,0,0,,and, well, I am the only \Nperson within 1,000 Miles
Dialogue: 0,00:13:38.82,00:13:42.07,Default,,0,0,0,,who knows how to properly code and \Ncatalog this library, that's why.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:42.15,00:13:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I put up with you because your father \Nand mother were our finest patrons.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:45.87,00:13:47.24,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why!
Dialogue: 0,00:13:47.53,00:13:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Allah rest their souls.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:50.87,00:13:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I don't care how you do it, \NI don't care how long it takes,
Dialogue: 0,00:13:54.62,00:13:57.09,Default,,0,0,0,,straighten up this meshiver!
Dialogue: 0,00:14:10.89,00:14:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello?
Dialogue: 0,00:14:38.17,00:14:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Abdul?
Dialogue: 0,00:14:41.63,00:14:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Mohammed?
Dialogue: 0,00:14:46.01,00:14:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Bob?
Dialogue: 0,00:15:07.66,00:15:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you no respect \Nfor the dead?
Dialogue: 0,00:15:12.41,00:15:16.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course I do. But sometimes \NI'd rather like to join them.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:17.08,00:15:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I wish you would do it before you \Nruin my career the way you've ruined yours.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:21.63,00:15:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- Now, get out. - My \Ndear, sweet baby sister.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:25.05,00:15:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll have you know
Dialogue: 0,00:15:27.30,00:15:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,that, at this precise moment, \Nmy career is on a high note.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:30.43,00:15:33.72,Default,,0,0,0,,High note, ha! Jonathan, please, I'm \Nreally not in the mood for you.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:33.81,00:15:36.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I've just made a bit of \Na mess in the library,
Dialogue: 0,00:15:36.31,00:15:39.23,Default,,0,0,0,,and the Bembridge scholars have \Nrejected my application form again.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:39.31,00:15:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,They say I don't have enough \Nexperience in the field.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:47.32,00:15:49.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll always have me, old mum.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:52.99,00:15:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, I have just the \Nthing to cheer you up.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:55.75,00:15:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, Jonathan, not \Nanother worthless trinket.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:59.25,00:16:02.25,Default,,0,0,0,,If I have to take one more piece \Nof junk to the curator to try and
Dialogue: 0,00:16:02.34,00:16:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,sell for you.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:07.72,00:16:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did you get this?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:10.26,00:16:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,On a dig down in Thebes.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:13.35,00:16:15.14,Default,,0,0,0,,My whole life, I've never \Nfound anything, Evy.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:15.18,00:16:17.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Please tell me I've \Nfound something.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:21.94,00:16:24.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- Jonathan. \N- Yes?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:25.32,00:16:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you've found something.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:31.53,00:16:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You see the cartouche there?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:33.03,00:16:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the official Royal seal of \NSETI the First, I'm sure of it.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:36.62,00:16:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- Perhaps. \N- Two questions.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:38.71,00:16:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Who the hell was SETI the \NFirst, and was he rich?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:41.54,00:16:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,He was the second pharaoh \Nof the 19th dynasty,
Dialogue: 0,00:16:43.96,00:16:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,said to be the wealthiest \Npharaoh of them all.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:45.80,00:16:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. I like this fellow.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:47.38,00:16:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- I like him very much. \N- I've already dated the map.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:49.88,00:16:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It's almost 3,000 years old.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:51.51,00:16:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you look at the hieratic \Njust here, well, it's Hamunaptra.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:56.22,00:16:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Dear God, don't be ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:58.89,00:17:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,We're scholars, not \Ntreasure hunters.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:01.39,00:17:04.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Hamunaptra's a myth told by \Nancient Arab storytellers
Dialogue: 0,00:17:04.61,00:17:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,to amuse Greek and \NRoman tourists.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:06.27,00:17:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I know all the blather about the city \Nbeing protected by the curse of a mummy,
Dialogue: 0,00:17:10.74,00:17:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,but my research has led me to believe that \Nthe city itself may have actually existed.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:15.58,00:17:19.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are we talking about the Hamunaptra? \N- Yes. The City of the Dead.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:19.79,00:17:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Where the earliest pharaohs were said \Nto have hidden the wealth of Egypt?
Dialogue: 0,00:17:23.04,00:17:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, yes, in a big, \Nunderground treasure chamber.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:26.42,00:17:29.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Heh! - Oh, come on. \N- Everybody knows the story.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:29.34,00:17:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The entire necropolis was rigged to sink \Ninto the sand on Pharaoh's command?
Dialogue: 0,00:17:32.18,00:17:35.18,Default,,0,0,0,,A flick of a switch, and the whole place \Nwould disappear beneath the sand dunes,
Dialogue: 0,00:17:35.26,00:17:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,taking the treasure with it?
Dialogue: 0,00:17:36.60,00:17:39.52,Default,,0,0,0,,As the Americans would say, \Nit's all fairy tales and hokum.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:39.60,00:17:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my goodness! Look at that!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:49.23,00:17:52.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You'be burnt it! You've burned \Noff the part with the lost city?
Dialogue: 0,00:17:52.32,00:17:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It's for the best, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:54.78,00:17:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Many men have wasted their lives in \Nthe foolish pursuit of Hamunaptra.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:58.91,00:18:00.100,Default,,0,0,0,,No one's ever found it.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:01.12,00:18:03.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Most have never returned.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:04.04,00:18:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, come! Step \Nover the threshold.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:06.71,00:18:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome to Cairo Prison, \Nmy humble home.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:09.46,00:18:12.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You told me that you got it \Non a dig down in Thebes.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:12.38,00:18:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, well, I was mistaken. \N- You lied to me.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:14.13,00:18:16.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I lie to everybody. What \Nmakes you so special?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:16.47,00:18:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,- I am your sister. - That \Njust makes you more gullible.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:18.64,00:18:20.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You stole it from a drunk \Nat the local casbah?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:20.60,00:18:23.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Picked his pocket, actually, so I \Ndon't think it's a very good...
Dialogue: 0,00:18:23.18,00:18:26.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop being so ridiculous. What \Nexactly is this man in prison for?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:26.40,00:18:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,This I did not know.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:28.23,00:18:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,But when I heard that you were \Ncoming, I asked him that myself.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:31.61,00:18:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,And what did he say?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:32.82,00:18:36.28,Default,,0,0,0,,He said he was just \Nlooking for a good time.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:41.99,00:18:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- This is the man that you \Nstole it from? - Yes, exactly?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:44.66,00:18:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So why don't we just go sniff \Nout a spot of tiff in...
Dialogue: 0,00:18:46.83,00:18:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:49.79,00:18:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,- And who's the broad? \N- "Broad"?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:51.55,00:18:55.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just a local sort of missionary \Nchap, spreading the good word,
Dialogue: 0,00:18:55.84,00:18:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- but this is my sister, Evy. \N- How do you do?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:59.35,00:19:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, well. Guess she's not a \Ntotal loss. - I beg your pardon?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:03.81,00:19:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back in a moment?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:05.02,00:19:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Ask him about the box. \N- We have found...
Dialogue: 0,00:19:08.69,00:19:10.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello. Excuse me?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:10.36,00:19:12.98,Default,,0,0,0,,We both found your puzzle box,
Dialogue: 0,00:19:13.44,00:19:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,and we've come to \Nask you about it?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:16.45,00:19:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- No. \N- No?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:18.70,00:19:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No. You came to ask \Nme about Hamunaptra.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:23.66,00:19:25.100,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know the box \Npertains to Hamunaptra?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:26.08,00:19:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Because that's where I was \Nwhen I found it. I was there.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:30.25,00:19:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But how do we know that's \Nnot a load of pig's wallow?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:33.71,00:19:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do I know you? \N- No, no.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:35.38,00:19:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I've just got one \Nof those faces.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:43.01,00:19:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You were actually at Hamunaptra?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:47.39,00:19:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, I was there. \N- You swear?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:49.23,00:19:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Every damn day. - I \Ndidn't mean that...
Dialogue: 0,00:19:51.06,00:19:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I know. I was there. SETI's \Nplace. City of the Dead.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:56.24,00:19:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Could you tell me \Nhow to get there?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:01.91,00:20:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, the exact location?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:04.66,00:20:07.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- You want to know? \N- Well, yes?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:07.25,00:20:09.71,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you really want to know? \N- Yes?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:13.63,00:20:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Then get me the \Nhell out of here!
Dialogue: 0,00:20:19.30,00:20:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Do it, lady!
Dialogue: 0,00:20:24.89,00:20:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where are they taking him? \N- To be hanged?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:27.98,00:20:30.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently, he had \Na very good time?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:36.36,00:20:38.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I will give you £100 to \Nsave this man's life.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:38.95,00:20:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Madame, I would pay £100 \Njust to see him hang.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:42.45,00:20:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- £200. \N- Proceed!
Dialogue: 0,00:20:44.49,00:20:45.62,Default,,0,0,0,,£300.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:47.37,00:20:49.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Any last requests, pig?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:49.79,00:20:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah? Loosen the \Nknot and let me go.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:56.30,00:20:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course we don't let him go!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:00.47,00:21:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,£500!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:03.97,00:21:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And what else? I'm \Na very lonely man.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:12.10,00:21:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:20.53,00:21:22.49,Default,,0,0,0,,His neck did not break.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:24.28,00:21:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I'm so sorry. Now, we must \Nwatch him strangle to death.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:37.29,00:21:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He knows the location \Nto Hamunaptra.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:40.55,00:21:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- You lie. \N- I would never!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:42.84,00:21:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me this \Nfilthy, godless son of a pig
Dialogue: 0,00:21:46.10,00:21:48.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- knows where to find the \NCity of the Dead? - Yes!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:48.31,00:21:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- Truly? \N- Yes!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:49.52,00:21:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you cut him down, \Nwe will give you...
Dialogue: 0,00:21:55.23,00:21:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- 10 % \N- 50 %
Dialogue: 0,00:21:56.98,00:21:58.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- Twenty. \N- Forty.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:58.69,00:22:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- Thirty! \N- Twenty five.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:01.07,00:22:02.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Deal.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:04.32,00:22:05.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut him down!
Dialogue: 0,00:22:16.96,00:22:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,GIZA PORT - CAIRO
Dialogue: 0,00:22:21.21,00:22:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you really think \Nhe's going to show up?
Dialogue: 0,00:22:23.09,00:22:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, undoubtedly, \Nknowing my luck.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:26.22,00:22:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,He may be a cowboy, but I know \Nthe breed. His word is his word.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:29.06,00:22:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, personally I think he's \Nfilthy, rude, a complete scoundrel.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:33.81,00:22:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,- I don't like him one bit. \N- Anyone I know?
Dialogue: 0,00:22:38.56,00:22:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:42.23,00:22:43.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:43.44,00:22:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Smashing day for the start of \Nan adventure, eh, O'Connell?
Dialogue: 0,00:22:46.24,00:22:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Yeah, smashing.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:48.70,00:22:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, no, I'd never steal \Nfrom a partner, partner.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:53.37,00:22:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,That reminds me? No hard \Nfeelings about the...
Dialogue: 0,00:22:55.96,00:22:59.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, no, no. Happens all \Nthe time. - Mr. O'Connell?
Dialogue: 0,00:22:59.25,00:23:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you look me in the \Neye and guarantee me
Dialogue: 0,00:23:01.09,00:23:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,this isn't some \Nsort of a flimflam?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:04.01,00:23:07.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- Because if it is, I am warning \Nyou... - You're warning me?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:07.64,00:23:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady, let me put it this way,
Dialogue: 0,00:23:09.30,00:23:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,my whole damn Garrison \Nbelieved in this so much
Dialogue: 0,00:23:11.85,00:23:14.64,Default,,0,0,0,,that without orders, they marched \Nhalfway across Libya and into Egypt
Dialogue: 0,00:23:14.73,00:23:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,to find that city.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:15.81,00:23:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,When we got there, all we \Nfound was sand and blood.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:20.86,00:23:22.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me get your bags.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:27.61,00:23:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, yes, you're right.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:29.78,00:23:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Filthy, rude, a complete scoundrel. \NNothing to like there at all.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:35.37,00:23:37.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Bright good morning to all.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:37.46,00:23:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no. What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:39.79,00:23:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm here to protect my \Ninvestment, thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:05.03,00:24:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit playing with your glasses \Nand cut the deck, Burns.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:08.15,00:24:11.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Without my glasses I can't see \Nthe deck to cut it, Dave.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:11.16,00:24:13.70,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell, sit down. We \Ncould use another player.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:13.78,00:24:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- I only gamble with my life, \Nnever my money. - Never?
Dialogue: 0,00:24:17.04,00:24:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I was to bet you $500 we \Nget to Hamunaptra before you?
Dialogue: 0,00:24:20.75,00:24:23.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're looking for Hamunaptra? \N- Damn straight we are.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:23.92,00:24:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- And who saya we are? \N- He does.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:26.67,00:24:29.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Well... Well, how about it?
Dialogue: 0,00:24:29.59,00:24:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it a bet?
Dialogue: 0,00:24:32.97,00:24:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- All right, you're on. - What \Nmakes you so confident, Sir?
Dialogue: 0,00:24:36.68,00:24:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- What makes you? - We got us a \Nman who's actually been there.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:40.02,00:24:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what a coincidence, \Nbecause O'Connell...
Dialogue: 0,00:24:43.06,00:24:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Whose play is it? Is it my play? \NI thought...
Dialogue: 0,00:24:45.90,00:24:49.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, we got us a wager. \NGood evening, Jonathan.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:49.70,00:24:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Night.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:06.42,00:25:08.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry. Didn't mean to scare you.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:08.42,00:25:11.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing that scares me, \NMr. O'Connell, are your manners.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:12.30,00:25:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- Still angry about that kiss, huh? \N- Well, if you call that a kiss.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:22.06,00:25:26.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I miss something? Are we... \NAre we going into battle?
Dialogue: 0,00:25:26.86,00:25:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Lady, there's \Nsomething out there.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:29.57,00:25:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Something underneath that sand.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:31.40,00:25:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, well, I'm hoping to \Nfind a certain artifact.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:34.91,00:25:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,A book, actually. My brother \Nthinks there's treasure.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:38.04,00:25:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- What do you think's out \Nthere? - In a word? Evil.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:42.92,00:25:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The Bedouin and the Tuaregs believe \Nthat Hamunaptra is cursed.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:46.50,00:25:49.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, look, I don't believe in fairy \Ntales and hokum, Mr. O'Connell,
Dialogue: 0,00:25:49.84,00:25:53.76,Default,,0,0,0,,but I do believe one of the most famous \Nbooks in history is buried there.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:53.84,00:25:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The Book of Amun-Ra.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:55.43,00:25:59.14,Default,,0,0,0,,It contains within it all the secret \Nincantations of the old kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:59.47,00:26:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It's what first interested me \Nin Egypt when I was a child.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:02.14,00:26:05.60,Default,,0,0,0,,It's why I came here. \NSort of a life's pursuit.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:05.77,00:26:09.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And the fact that they say it's made out \Nof pure gold makes no never mind to you?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:10.48,00:26:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Right. - You \Nknow your history.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:12.32,00:26:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I know my treasure.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:18.58,00:26:20.08,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way,
Dialogue: 0,00:26:20.100,00:26:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,why did you kiss me?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:22.62,00:26:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I was about to be hanged. It seemed \Nlike a good idea at the time.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:29.63,00:26:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,What? What'd I say?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:40.01,00:26:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Surprise! My good \Nfriend, you're alive!
Dialogue: 0,00:26:43.02,00:26:47.31,Default,,0,0,0,,- I was so very, very worried. - Well, \Nif it ain't my little buddy, Beni.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:48.02,00:26:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- I think I'll kill you. \N- Think of my children.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:50.40,00:26:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have any children.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:52.40,00:26:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- Someday I might. \N- Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,00:26:54.49,00:26:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,So, you're the one who's \Nleading the Americans?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:56.91,00:26:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I might have known. So, \Nwhat's the scam, Beni?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:58.95,00:27:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You task them into the middle of the \Ndesert, and then you leave them to rot?
Dialogue: 0,00:27:02.45,00:27:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, no.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:04.41,00:27:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,These Americans are smart.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:06.50,00:27:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They pay me only half now, half \Nwhen I get them back to Cairo.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:09.59,00:27:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- So this time I must go all the \Nway. - Them's the breaks, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:27:13.92,00:27:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You never believed in \NHamunaptra, O'Connell.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:17.38,00:27:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you going back?
Dialogue: 0,00:27:21.22,00:27:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You see that girl? \NShe saved my neck.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:28.90,00:27:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You always did have \Nmore balls than brains.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:37.20,00:27:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah. Goodbye, Beni.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:46.29,00:27:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,00:28:00.09,00:28:01.89,Default,,0,0,0,,George Bembridge...
Dialogue: 0,00:28:02.60,00:28:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,In 1860...
Dialogue: 0,00:28:08.48,00:28:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,1865, was...
Dialogue: 0,00:28:13.61,00:28:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Was...
Dialogue: 0,00:28:14.86,00:28:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, for heaven's sake, girl, it \Nwasn't that good of a kiss, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:32.79,00:28:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is the map?
Dialogue: 0,00:28:35.75,00:28:38.26,Default,,0,0,0,,It's... It's... There.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:38.47,00:28:41.26,Default,,0,0,0,,And the key? Where is the key?
Dialogue: 0,00:28:41.76,00:28:44.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The key? The key? What key?
Dialogue: 0,00:28:44.43,00:28:45.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn!
Dialogue: 0,00:29:01.57,00:29:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,The map! The map! \NI forgot the map!
Dialogue: 0,00:29:03.70,00:29:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Relax. I'm the map? \NIt's all up here?
Dialogue: 0,00:29:07.08,00:29:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's comforting.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:16.96,00:29:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- The key! \N- Evy.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:39.78,00:29:41.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on to this.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:10.18,00:30:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you swim?
Dialogue: 0,00:30:11.43,00:30:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course I can swim, if \Nthe occasion calls for it.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:14.19,00:30:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Trust me. It calls for it.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:40.21,00:30:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell! O'Connell! \NWhat are we going to do?
Dialogue: 0,00:30:43.38,00:30:45.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Wait here! I'll go get help! \N- Right!
Dialogue: 0,00:31:08.37,00:31:09.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Americans.
Dialogue: 0,00:31:25.09,00:31:27.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I say, bloody good show, chaps!
Dialogue: 0,00:31:28.55,00:31:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And did I panic?
Dialogue: 0,00:31:30.39,00:31:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I think not.
Dialogue: 0,00:31:44.23,00:31:46.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Get them out of the water! \NGet them out of the water!
Dialogue: 0,00:31:46.82,00:31:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, doggies! Give \Nthem a smack, would you?
Dialogue: 0,00:31:53.37,00:31:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a messed-up country.
Dialogue: 0,00:31:58.54,00:32:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We've lost everything! All of \Nour tools, all the equipment!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:02.71,00:32:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,All my clothes!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:03.96,00:32:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:06.84,00:32:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:08.47,00:32:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:10.22,00:32:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks to me like I've \Ngot all the horses!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:14.64,00:32:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Beni!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:16.10,00:32:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks to me like you're on \Nthe wrong side of the river!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:20.31,00:32:21.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,00:32:38.100,00:32:41.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I only want four! Four!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:41.33,00:32:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I only want four, not \Na whole bloody herd!
Dialogue: 0,00:32:44.00,00:32:47.34,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell! Can you \Nbelieve the cheek?
Dialogue: 0,00:32:47.42,00:32:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Just pay the man.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:49.34,00:32:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, for heaven's sake.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:52.09,00:32:54.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't believe the price \Nof these fleabags?
Dialogue: 0,00:32:54.47,00:32:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, happy? Very good.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:58.02,00:33:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You probably could've \Ngot them for free.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:00.19,00:33:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- All we had to do was give \Nhim your sister. - Yes.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:03.65,00:33:05.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Awfully tempting, wasn't it?
Dialogue: 0,00:33:12.49,00:33:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Awfully.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:39.14,00:33:40.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Never did like camels.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:40.89,00:33:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Filthy buggers. They smell, \Nthey bite, they spit.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:45.15,00:33:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- Disgusting. - I think \Nthey're adorable.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:50.40,00:33:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, baby.
Dialogue: 0,00:35:40.51,00:35:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,This one is strong.
Dialogue: 0,00:35:51.52,00:35:53.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, my friend.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:09.71,00:36:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell we doing?
Dialogue: 0,00:36:10.88,00:36:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Patience, my good barat'm. \NPatience.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:13.84,00:36:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember our bet, O'Connell? First \None to the city, 500 cash bucks.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:18.68,00:36:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,A hundred of them bucks is yours \Nif you help us win that bet.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:21.22,00:36:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:23.39,00:36:26.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, O'Connell. Nice camel.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:30.98,00:36:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Get ready for it.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:33.48,00:36:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- For what? - We're about \Nto be shown the way.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:50.42,00:36:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- Will you look at that? \N- Can you believe it?
Dialogue: 0,00:36:54.29,00:36:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hamunaptra.
Dialogue: 0,00:36:55.75,00:36:57.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Here we go again.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:31.75,00:37:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,So long, Beni!
Dialogue: 0,00:37:36.42,00:37:38.30,Default,,0,0,0,,That serves you right.
Dialogue: 0,00:38:04.24,00:38:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Evy! Go!
Dialogue: 0,00:38:47.70,00:38:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Do they know something we don't?
Dialogue: 0,00:38:50.54,00:38:53.79,Default,,0,0,0,,They are led by a woman. \NWhat does a woman know?
Dialogue: 0,00:38:54.21,00:38:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a statue of Anubis.
Dialogue: 0,00:38:56.54,00:38:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's legs go deep underground.
Dialogue: 0,00:38:58.25,00:39:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,According to Bembridge scholars, that's \Nwhere we'll find a secret compartment
Dialogue: 0,00:39:02.30,00:39:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,containing the Golden \NBook of Amun-Ra.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:07.09,00:39:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Jonathan, you're meant to \Ncatch the sun with that.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:12.06,00:39:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- So, what are these old mirrors \Nfor? - Ancient mirrors.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:16.06,00:39:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It's an ancient Egyptian trick. \NYou'll see.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:20.23,00:39:22.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, this for you.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:24.40,00:39:27.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead. It's something I borrowed \Noff our American brethren.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:27.61,00:39:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you might like it, you \Nmight need it for when you're...
Dialogue: 0,00:39:31.24,00:39:34.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah? What are you looking at?
Dialogue: 0,00:39:44.92,00:39:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, look for bugs. I hate bugs.
Dialogue: 0,00:39:48.55,00:39:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you realize we're \Nstanding inside a room
Dialogue: 0,00:39:50.93,00:39:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,no one has entered \Nin over 3,000 years?
Dialogue: 0,00:39:54.22,00:39:56.60,Default,,0,0,0,,What is that God-awful stench?
Dialogue: 0,00:40:06.90,00:40:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And then there was light?
Dialogue: 0,00:40:11.83,00:40:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, that is a neat trick.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:14.29,00:40:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, my God. It's a \Nsah-netjer. - What?
Dialogue: 0,00:40:16.100,00:40:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- A preparation room. \N- Preparation for what?
Dialogue: 0,00:40:19.50,00:40:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,For entering the afterlife.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:23.13,00:40:25.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Mummies, my good son. This is \Nwhere they made the mummies.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:49.36,00:40:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The legs of Anubis.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:52.28,00:40:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,The secret compartment should be \Nhidden somewhere inside here.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:21.69,00:41:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You scared the bejesus \Nout of us, O'Connell.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:23.94,00:41:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Likewise.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:25.32,00:41:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey, that's my tool Kit. \N- No, I don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:28.57,00:41:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay? Perhaps I was mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:32.99,00:41:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Have a nice day, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:34.62,00:41:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We have a lot of work to \Nbe getting along with.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:36.66,00:41:39.100,Default,,0,0,0,,- Push off! This is our dig \Nsite? - We got here first.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:41.100,00:41:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,This here's our statue, friend.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:44.42,00:41:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't see your name \Nwritten on it, pal.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:47.46,00:41:50.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, well, there's \Nonly four of you
Dialogue: 0,00:41:50.84,00:41:52.84,Default,,0,0,0,,and 15 of me.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:53.05,00:41:55.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Your odds are not so \Ngreat, O'Connell.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:56.18,00:41:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- I've had worse. \N- Yeah, me, too.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:00.18,00:42:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, look, for goodness' sake, \Nlet's be nice, children.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:04.19,00:42:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,If we're going to play together, \Nwe must learn to share.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:09.98,00:42:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,There are other places to dig.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:16.53,00:42:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,According to these hieroglyphics, \Nwe're underneath the statue.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:20.41,00:42:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We should come up right \Nbetween his legs.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:22.29,00:42:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,When those damn Yanks \Ngo to sleep...
Dialogue: 0,00:42:24.29,00:42:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- No offense. \N- None taken.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:25.92,00:42:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll dig our way up \Nand steal that book
Dialogue: 0,00:42:27.42,00:42:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,right out from under them?
Dialogue: 0,00:42:28.50,00:42:30.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure we can find \Nthis secret compartment?
Dialogue: 0,00:42:30.96,00:42:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, if those beastly Americans \Nhaven't beaten us to it.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:33.93,00:42:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- No offense. \N- None taken.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:35.68,00:42:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Where'd our smelly \Nlittle friend get to?
Dialogue: 0,00:42:46.56,00:42:47.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me get this straight.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:47.98,00:42:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,They ripped out your guts \Nand stuffed them in jars?
Dialogue: 0,00:42:50.48,00:42:54.07,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd take out your heart as well. You \Nknow how they took out your brains?
Dialogue: 0,00:42:54.15,00:42:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think we \Nneed to know this.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:55.86,00:42:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,They'd take a sharp, red-hot \Npoker, stick it up your nose,
Dialogue: 0,00:42:59.49,00:43:03.08,Default,,0,0,0,,scramble things asbout a bit, and then \Nrip it all out through your nostrils.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:03.16,00:43:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's gotta hurt. - It's \Ncalled mummification.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:05.58,00:43:07.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- You'll be dead when they \Ndo this. - For the record,
Dialogue: 0,00:43:07.75,00:43:10.80,Default,,0,0,0,,if I don't make it out of here, don't \Nput me down for mummification.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:10.88,00:43:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Likewise.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:21.35,00:43:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God. It's a...
Dialogue: 0,00:43:24.02,00:43:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a sarcophagus.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:28.52,00:43:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Buried at the base of Anubis.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:32.86,00:43:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,He must have been someone \Nof great importance.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:37.07,00:43:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Or he did something \Nvery naughty.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:42.41,00:43:44.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, who is it?
Dialogue: 0,00:43:46.21,00:43:48.67,Default,,0,0,0,,"He That Shall Not Be Named."
Dialogue: 0,00:43:53.34,00:43:55.26,Default,,0,0,0,,This looks like some \Nsort of a lock.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:55.34,00:43:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, whoever's in here \Nsure wasn't getting out.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:57.51,00:43:59.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, no kidding.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:59.22,00:44:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,It'd take us a month to crack \Ninto this thing without a key.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:02.31,00:44:03.51,Default,,0,0,0,,A key?
Dialogue: 0,00:44:04.22,00:44:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,A key! A key! That's what \Nhe was talking about!
Dialogue: 0,00:44:07.35,00:44:10.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who? \N- The man on the barge,
Dialogue: 0,00:44:10.10,00:44:12.02,Default,,0,0,0,,the one with the hook. He \Nwas looking for a key.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:12.11,00:44:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, that's mine.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:18.86,00:44:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Seems that our American friends had a \Nlittle misfortune of their own today.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:23.08,00:44:26.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Three of their \Ndiggers were melted.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:26.83,00:44:28.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- What? \N- How?
Dialogue: 0,00:44:28.79,00:44:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Salt acid.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:30.71,00:44:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Pressurized salt acid. Some \Nkind of ancient booby trap.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:36.17,00:44:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe this place \Nreally is cursed.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:41.97,00:44:44.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, for goodness' sake, you two!
Dialogue: 0,00:44:44.51,00:44:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- You don't believe in curses? \N- No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:46.81,00:44:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe if I can see it and I can touch \Nit, it's real. That's what I believe.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:51.23,00:44:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe in being prepared.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:56.15,00:44:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Take this. Stay here.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:58.86,00:45:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- No, wait, wait! Wait \Nfor me. Wait! - Evy!
Dialogue: 0,00:45:01.74,00:45:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, but didn't the \Nman just say stay here?
Dialogue: 0,00:45:04.99,00:45:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Evy!
Dialogue: 0,00:45:09.12,00:45:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Henderson! Wake up!
Dialogue: 0,00:45:51.71,00:45:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,00:46:12.56,00:46:13.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough!
Dialogue: 0,00:46:15.27,00:46:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,We will shed no more \Nblood, but you must leave?
Dialogue: 0,00:46:19.23,00:46:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave this place or die.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:22.28,00:46:23.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You have one day.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:47.72,00:46:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:51.27,00:46:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:54.23,00:46:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you all right? \N- Yes, I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:57.94,00:46:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- You sure? \N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:59.52,00:47:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That proves it. Old SETI's fortune's \Ngot to be under this sand.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:03.61,00:47:06.61,Default,,0,0,0,,For them to protect it like this, you \Nknow there's treasure down there.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:06.70,00:47:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No, these men are desert people. \NThey value water, not gold.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:11.16,00:47:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, maybe just at night, \Nwe could combine forces.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:17.71,00:47:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, tough stuff, \Ntry a right hook.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:19.79,00:47:22.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Ball up your fist and put it... \NPut it up like that.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:22.63,00:47:24.38,Default,,0,0,0,,And then mean it. \NHit it right here.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:24.47,00:47:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mean it! \N- Okay.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:29.51,00:47:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, it's time for \Nanother drink.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:32.35,00:47:34.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Unlike my brother, Sir,
Dialogue: 0,00:47:35.48,00:47:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I know when to say no.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:40.15,00:47:42.40,Default,,0,0,0,,And unlike your brother, miss,
Dialogue: 0,00:47:42.48,00:47:44.36,Default,,0,0,0,,you, I just don't get.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:46.32,00:47:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I know. You're wondering
Dialogue: 0,00:47:50.41,00:47:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,what is a place like me \Ndoing in a girl like this.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:54.87,00:47:58.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, something like that. \N- Egypt is in my blood.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:59.33,00:48:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You see,
Dialogue: 0,00:48:00.67,00:48:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,my father was a very, \Nvery famous explorer.
Dialogue: 0,00:48:05.59,00:48:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And he loved Egypt so much,
Dialogue: 0,00:48:08.01,00:48:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,he married my mother, \Nwho was an Egyptian
Dialogue: 0,00:48:11.68,00:48:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and quite an adventurer herself?
Dialogue: 0,00:48:15.85,00:48:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I get your father and I \Nget your mother, and...
Dialogue: 0,00:48:21.23,00:48:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I get him, but...
Dialogue: 0,00:48:24.23,00:48:26.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,00:48:27.61,00:48:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I may not be an explorer
Dialogue: 0,00:48:32.28,00:48:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,or an adventurer or \Na treasure seeker
Dialogue: 0,00:48:36.66,00:48:39.87,Default,,0,0,0,,or a gunfighter, Mr. O'Connell,
Dialogue: 0,00:48:40.58,00:48:45.25,Default,,0,0,0,,but I am proud of what I am.
Dialogue: 0,00:48:46.05,00:48:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And what is that?
Dialogue: 0,00:48:47.80,00:48:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,00:48:51.09,00:48:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,am a librarian.
Dialogue: 0,00:48:57.22,00:49:00.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And I am going to kiss you,
Dialogue: 0,00:49:00.52,00:49:02.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mr. O'Connell. \N- Call me Rick.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:09.45,00:49:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Rick.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:47.11,00:49:49.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- There is a curse upon this \Nchest. - Curse, my ass.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:49.94,00:49:52.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who cares? - Have a \Ncare, Mr. Henderson.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:52.78,00:49:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,In these hallowed grounds, that which \Nwas set forth in ancient times
Dialogue: 0,00:49:55.95,00:49:58.41,Default,,0,0,0,,- is as strong today as it \Nwas then. - We understand.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:58.49,00:50:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What's it say?
Dialogue: 0,00:50:07.63,00:50:10.21,Default,,0,0,0,,"Death will come on swift wings"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:10.30,00:50:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,"to whomsoever \Nopens this chest."
Dialogue: 0,00:50:24.48,00:50:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,We should not be here.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:27.19,00:50:28.77,Default,,0,0,0,,This is not good.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:28.86,00:50:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It says,
Dialogue: 0,00:50:30.32,00:50:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,"There is one, the undead,"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:32.95,00:50:36.32,Default,,0,0,0,,"who, if brought back to life, \Nis bound by sacred law"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:36.41,00:50:38.37,Default,,0,0,0,,"to consummate this curse."
Dialogue: 0,00:50:38.45,00:50:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's make sure we don't bring \Nanyone back from the dead then.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:41.37,00:50:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,"He will kill all who \Nopen this chest"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:44.83,00:50:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,"and assimilate their \Norgans and fluids,"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:49.05,00:50:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,"and in so doing, \Nhe will regenerate"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:51.92,00:50:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,"and no longer be the undead,"
Dialogue: 0,00:50:54.68,00:50:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,"but a plague upon this Earth."
Dialogue: 0,00:50:59.10,00:51:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we didn't come all \Nthis way for nothing.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:02.35,00:51:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's right. \N- It's the curse.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:04.89,00:51:06.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the curse.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:06.52,00:51:10.32,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the curse! \NBeware of the curse!
Dialogue: 0,00:51:10.40,00:51:11.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Beware!
Dialogue: 0,00:51:12.03,00:51:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Stupid superstitious bastard.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:17.07,00:51:19.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I've dreamt about this \Nsince I was a little girl.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:19.87,00:51:21.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You dream about dead guys?
Dialogue: 0,00:51:21.37,00:51:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, the sacred spells \Nhave been chiseled off.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:24.83,00:51:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,This man must have been condemned not \Nonly in this life, but in the next.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:28.04,00:51:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- Tough break. - Yeah, \NI'm all tears.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:30.29,00:51:33.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, let's see who's \Ninside, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,00:51:44.31,00:51:46.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God, I hate it when \Nthese things do that.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:47.06,00:51:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he supposed to \Nlook like that?
Dialogue: 0,00:51:48.60,00:51:51.02,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I've never seen a mummy \Nlook like this before.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:51.11,00:51:53.86,Default,,0,0,0,,He's still... Still...
Dialogue: 0,00:51:53.94,00:51:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- Juicy. \N- Juicy.
Dialogue: 0,00:51:55.07,00:51:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:04.70,00:52:06.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:06.87,00:52:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,It does exist.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:08.96,00:52:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- The Book of the Dead. \N- A book?
Dialogue: 0,00:52:12.38,00:52:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Who cares about a book? Where \Nthe hell's the treasure?
Dialogue: 0,00:52:15.09,00:52:16.72,Default,,0,0,0,,This, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:17.93,00:52:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,This is treasure.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:21.55,00:52:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, I wouldn't trade \Nyou for a brass...
Dialogue: 0,00:52:27.10,00:52:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at that.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:30.06,00:52:32.31,Default,,0,0,0,,There's your \Ntreasure, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:32.40,00:52:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, we're on to something.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:50.37,00:52:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe you need a \Nkey to open that book.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:55.38,00:52:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Say, O'Connell,
Dialogue: 0,00:52:56.59,00:52:59.01,Default,,0,0,0,,what do you think these \Nbabies'll fetch back home?
Dialogue: 0,00:52:59.09,00:53:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We hear you boys found yourselves a \Nnice, gooey mummy. Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:03.30,00:53:07.64,Default,,0,0,0,,If you dry that fellow out, you might \Nbe able to sell him for firewood.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:38.46,00:53:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That's called \Nstealing, you know?
Dialogue: 0,00:53:40.76,00:53:44.51,Default,,0,0,0,,According to you and my \Nbrother, it's called borrowing.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:47.10,00:53:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought the Book of Amun-Ra \Nwas made out of gold?
Dialogue: 0,00:53:50.14,00:53:54.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It is made out of gold. This \Nisn't the Book of Amun-Ra.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:54.15,00:53:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,This is something else.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:56.44,00:53:59.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I think this may be \Nthe Book of the Dead.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:59.65,00:54:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The Book of the Dead?
Dialogue: 0,00:54:01.45,00:54:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you're meant to be \Nplaying around with this thing?
Dialogue: 0,00:54:03.86,00:54:05.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just a book.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:05.87,00:54:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No harm ever came \Nfrom reading a book.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:15.29,00:54:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That happens a lot around here.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:20.17,00:54:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,So, what's it say?
Dialogue: 0,00:54:21.63,00:54:24.76,Default,,0,0,0,,"Amun Ra. Amun Dei."
Dialogue: 0,00:54:25.59,00:54:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It speaks of the night \Nand of the day.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:42.40,00:54:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,No! You must not \Nread from the book!
Dialogue: 0,00:55:12.85,00:55:14.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,00:55:16.69,00:55:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, go!
Dialogue: 0,00:55:26.82,00:55:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,What have we done?
Dialogue: 0,00:55:30.12,00:55:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where the hell did they come from? \N- I ain't waiting around to find out.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:41.00,00:55:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Jon!
Dialogue: 0,00:55:48.72,00:55:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Scarabs!
Dialogue: 0,00:55:50.35,00:55:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Run, Evy! Go, go, go! Run!
Dialogue: 0,00:56:09.62,00:56:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you to leave or die.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:12.28,00:56:13.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You refused.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:14.04,00:56:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, you may have killed us all,
Dialogue: 0,00:56:16.04,00:56:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,for you have unleashed a creasture we \Nhave feared for more than 3,000 years.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:22.96,00:56:26.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I must now go on the hunt, and \Ntry and find a way to kill him.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:59.21,00:57:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,May the good Lord protect \Nand watch over me
Dialogue: 0,00:57:02.84,00:57:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,as a Shepherd watches \Nover his flock.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:19.18,00:57:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No. Okay.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:40.79,00:57:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The language of the slaves...
Dialogue: 0,00:57:44.13,00:57:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I may have use for you.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:48.76,00:57:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And the rewards...
Dialogue: 0,00:57:51.63,00:57:54.30,Default,,0,0,0,,will be great.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:56.01,00:57:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,My Prince.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:00.48,00:58:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are the other \Nsacred jars...
Dialogue: 0,00:58:26.08,00:58:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you said you didn't believe \Nin that fairy tales and hokum stuff.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:29.46,00:58:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Having an encounter with a \N3,000-year-old walking, talking corpse
Dialogue: 0,00:58:33.93,00:58:35.26,Default,,0,0,0,,does tend to convert one.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:35.34,00:58:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Forget it. We're out the door, \Ndown the hall, and we're gone.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:38.76,00:58:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, no, we are not. \N- Oh, yes, we are.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:41.93,00:58:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, we are not. We woke him \Nup, and we are going to stop him.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:44.77,00:58:46.86,Default,,0,0,0,,We? What we? We didn't \Nread that book.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:46.94,00:58:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you not to play around with \Nthat thing. Didn't I tell you?
Dialogue: 0,00:58:49.69,00:58:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, right then, me, me, me, me. I, I, I \Nwoke him up and I intend to stop him.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:52.95,00:58:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah? How?
Dialogue: 0,00:58:54.45,00:58:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You heard the man. No mortal \Nweapons can kill this guy.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:57.16,00:59:00.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we are just going to have \Nto find some immortal ones.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:00.45,00:59:01.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There goes that we again.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:01.100,00:59:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, will you listen to me? \NWe have to do something.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:04.46,00:59:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Once this creature has been reborn, \Nhis curse is going to spread
Dialogue: 0,00:59:07.17,00:59:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,until the whole of the \NEarth is destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:08.79,00:59:11.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah? Is that my problem? \N- Lt is everybody's problem.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:11.88,00:59:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn, I appreciate you \Nsaving my life and all,
Dialogue: 0,00:59:14.26,00:59:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,but when I signed on, I agreed to take \Nyou out there and to bring you back.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:17.64,00:59:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I have done that? End of job. End \Nof story. Contract terminated.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:21.06,00:59:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all I am to you? \NA contract?
Dialogue: 0,00:59:22.35,00:59:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You can either tag along with me or you \Ncan stay here and try and save the world.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:27.48,00:59:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's it gonna be? \N- I'm staying.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:30.02,00:59:33.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- Fine. \N- Fine.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:33.32,00:59:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:40.70,00:59:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm the last of the Royal Air Corps \Nstill stationed out here, you know...
Dialogue: 0,00:59:45.16,00:59:47.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Some bloody idiot \Nspilt his drink.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:48.17,00:59:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,All the other laddies died in the \Nsky and were buried in the sand.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:52.21,00:59:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Good chaps, every \None of them, too.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:55.01,00:59:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi, Winston. \N- Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,00:59:57.72,01:00:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, O'Connell, ever since \Nthe end of the great war,
Dialogue: 0,01:00:01.47,01:00:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,there hasn't been a single \Nchallenge worthy of a man like me.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:06.69,01:00:09.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah? We all got our little \Nproblems today, Winston.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:09.23,01:00:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I just wish I could have \Nchucked it in with the others
Dialogue: 0,01:00:12.77,01:00:14.94,Default,,0,0,0,,and gone down in \Nflame and Glory,
Dialogue: 0,01:00:15.03,01:00:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,instead of sitting \Naround here, rotting
Dialogue: 0,01:00:17.53,01:00:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- of boredom and booze. \N- Of boredom and booze.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:19.20,01:00:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheers.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:23.29,01:00:25.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well, back to the airfield.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:27.54,01:00:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- Tell me, has your sister always \Nbeen... - Oh, yes, always.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:30.21,01:00:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We're all packed up, but the damn boat \Ndoesn't leave till tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:33.30,01:00:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Tail set firmly between \Nyour legs, I see.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:35.71,01:00:39.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You can talk. You don't have some \Nsacred walking corpse after you.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:41.30,01:00:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweet Jesus!
Dialogue: 0,01:00:43.60,01:00:45.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Tasted just like...
Dialogue: 0,01:00:46.52,01:00:47.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Blood.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:47.98,01:00:53.40,Default,,0,0,0,,"And the rivers and waters of \NEgypt ran red and were as blood."
Dialogue: 0,01:00:55.57,01:00:57.19,Default,,0,0,0,,He's here.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:01.70,01:01:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, looks like it's gonna storm.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:03.70,01:01:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, Evelyn! - Oh, \Nso you're still here.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:07.58,01:01:09.37,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got problems.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:31.90,01:01:33.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,01:01:33.90,01:01:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Beni, you little stinkweed. \NWhere you been?
Dialogue: 0,01:02:02.01,01:02:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,We are in serious trouble.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:22.28,01:02:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You saved me from the undead.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:23.86,01:02:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I thank you.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:41.47,01:02:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,We are in very serious trouble.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:46.64,01:02:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- He does seem to like you Evy. \N- Yeah, what's that about?
Dialogue: 0,01:02:48.97,01:02:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this guy want?
Dialogue: 0,01:02:50.27,01:02:53.35,Default,,0,0,0,,There's only one person that \Ncan give us any answers.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:53.48,01:02:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- You! \N- Miss Carnahan.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:56.52,01:02:59.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Gentlemen. - What \Nis he doing here?
Dialogue: 0,01:02:59.57,01:03:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you really want to know, or \Nwould you prefer to just shoot us?
Dialogue: 0,01:03:03.32,01:03:07.32,Default,,0,0,0,,After what I just saw, I'm willing \Nto go on a little faith here.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:07.41,01:03:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,We are part of an \Nancient secret society.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:10.08,01:03:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,For over 3,000 yeasrs, we have \Nguarded the City of the Dead.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:13.87,01:03:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We are sworn at manhood to do any and all \Nin our part to stop the High Priest Imhotep
Dialogue: 0,01:03:18.25,01:03:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,from being reborn \Ninto this world.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:19.84,01:03:21.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Because of you, we have failed.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:21.51,01:03:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You think this justifies the \Nkilling of innocent people.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:24.17,01:03:26.09,Default,,0,0,0,,To stop this creature? \NLet me think.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:26.18,01:03:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes! \N- Yes!
Dialogue: 0,01:03:29.14,01:03:31.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Question. Why doesn't \Nhe like cats?
Dialogue: 0,01:03:31.97,01:03:33.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Cats are the guardians \Nof the underworld.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:33.98,01:03:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,He will fear them until \Nhe is fully regenerated?
Dialogue: 0,01:03:35.89,01:03:37.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he will fear nothing.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:37.23,01:03:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You know how he gets his \Nself fully regenerated?
Dialogue: 0,01:03:39.19,01:03:43.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- By killing everyone who opened \Nthat chest. - And sucking them dry!
Dialogue: 0,01:03:43.36,01:03:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Jonathan, will you stop \Nplaying with that.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:45.82,01:03:50.62,Default,,0,0,0,,When I saw him alive at Hamunaptra, \Nhe called me Anck-Su-Namun.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:52.54,01:03:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,And then juat now in Mr. Burns' \Nquarters, he tried to kiss me.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:55.75,01:03:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It's because of his love for \NAnck-Su-Namun that he was cursed.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:58.75,01:04:01.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- Apparently, even after 3,000 years... \N- He is still in love with her.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:01.75,01:04:04.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, that is very romantic, but \Nwhat has it got to do with me?
Dialogue: 0,01:04:04.38,01:04:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps he will once again try \Nto raise her from the dead.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:06.72,01:04:07.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:07.84,01:04:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And it appears he has already \Nchosen his human sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:13.89,01:04:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Bad luck, old mum.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:15.81,01:04:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,On the contrary,
Dialogue: 0,01:04:17.56,01:04:21.23,Default,,0,0,0,,it may just give us the time \Nwe need to kill the creature.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:21.31,01:04:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We will need all the \Nhelp we can get.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:24.69,01:04:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,His powers are growing.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:31.41,01:04:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,"And he stretched forth his \Nhand towards the heavens"
Dialogue: 0,01:04:35.16,01:04:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,"and there was darkness \Nthroughout the land of Egypt."
Dialogue: 0,01:04:39.87,01:04:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We must stop him \Nfrom regenerating.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:41.59,01:04:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Who opened that chest?
Dialogue: 0,01:04:42.75,01:04:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,There was me and Daniels here.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:44.38,01:04:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- And Burns, of course. - And \Nthat Egyptologist fellow.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:46.80,01:04:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,What about my buddy, Beni?
Dialogue: 0,01:04:48.05,01:04:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he scrammed out of there \Nbefore we opened the thing.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:50.39,01:04:53.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, he was the smart one. \N- Yeah, that sounds like Beni.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:53.43,01:04:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,We must find the Egyptologist and bring \Nhim back to the safety of the fort
Dialogue: 0,01:04:56.89,01:04:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- before the creature can \Nget to him. - Right.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:59.14,01:05:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,She stays here. You \Nthree, come with me.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:00.81,01:05:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- Not me... \N- No, no!
Dialogue: 0,01:05:02.77,01:05:06.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a minute! You can't leave me \Nbehind like some old carpetbag.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:06.78,01:05:10.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Who put you in charge, O'Connell? \NWhat do you think you are doing?
Dialogue: 0,01:05:10.20,01:05:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Jonathan! O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,01:05:11.82,01:05:14.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sorry, but he's a bit tall. \N- Jonathan, coward that you are...
Dialogue: 0,01:05:14.70,01:05:17.16,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell, you are not \Nleaving me in here!
Dialogue: 0,01:05:17.70,01:05:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Jonathan, if you don't open \Nthis door in one minute flat...
Dialogue: 0,01:05:20.67,01:05:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- O'Connell... - This \Ndoor doesn't open.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:22.71,01:05:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let me out of here. \N- She doesn't come out,
Dialogue: 0,01:05:24.29,01:05:26.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- and no one goes in, right? \N- Right.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:26.34,01:05:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- Right? \N- Right.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:28.09,01:05:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell! Jonathan!
Dialogue: 0,01:05:30.34,01:05:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Jonathan?
Dialogue: 0,01:05:31.68,01:05:34.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I thought I could just astay \Nat the fort and reconnoiter.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:34.89,01:05:36.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Now! \N- Yeah, right.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:36.26,01:05:38.73,Default,,0,0,0,,We're just gonna rescue \Nthe Egyptologist.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:11.51,01:06:15.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, well, well. Let me guess. \NSpring cleaning?
Dialogue: 0,01:06:19.35,01:06:20.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice shot.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:21.52,01:06:24.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Beni, did you fall down? \NLet me help you up.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:27.07,01:06:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You came back from the desert with \Na new friend, didn't you, Beni?
Dialogue: 0,01:06:30.74,01:06:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What friend? You are \Nmy only friend.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:35.62,01:06:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell are you doing with \Nthis creep? What's in it for you?
Dialogue: 0,01:06:39.54,01:06:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It is better to be the right hand \Nof the devil than in his path.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:43.62,01:06:46.88,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as I serve \Nhim, I am immune.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:50.55,01:06:51.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Immune from what?
Dialogue: 0,01:06:53.47,01:06:54.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you say?
Dialogue: 0,01:06:54.63,01:06:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't wanna tell you. You'll \Njust hurt me some more.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:57.55,01:07:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you looking for? \NAnd try not to lie to me.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:00.81,01:07:02.14,Default,,0,0,0,,The book!
Dialogue: 0,01:07:02.23,01:07:05.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The black book they found at \NHamunaptra. He wants it back.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:05.48,01:07:07.65,Default,,0,0,0,,He said to me it would be \Nworth it's weight in gold.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:07.73,01:07:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- What does he want the \Nbook for? - I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:10.90,01:07:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Something about bringing his \Ndead girlfriend back to life.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:14.40,01:07:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's all. He just \Nwants the book, I swear.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:16.91,01:07:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Just the book, I swear. \NAnd your sister.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:20.45,01:07:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But other than that...
Dialogue: 0,01:08:12.63,01:08:16.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's two down, two to go. \N- Then he'll be coming after Evy.
Dialogue: 0,01:08:16.67,01:08:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Guards in place!
Dialogue: 0,01:08:18.30,01:08:19.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Reporting all clear, Sir!
Dialogue: 0,01:08:19.93,01:08:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,To hell with this?
Dialogue: 0,01:08:21.51,01:08:23.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going downstairs, get me \Na drink. You want something?
Dialogue: 0,01:08:24.02,01:08:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah. Yeah, get me a glass \Nof bourbon. - All right.
Dialogue: 0,01:08:27.31,01:08:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- And a shot of bourbon. \N- Yeah, okay, okay.
Dialogue: 0,01:08:29.69,01:08:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- And as bourbon chasser. \N- I'll get your damn bourbon!
Dialogue: 0,01:08:32.32,01:08:34.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about the door.
Dialogue: 0,01:10:13.92,01:10:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Anck-Su-Namun.
Dialogue: 0,01:10:26.85,01:10:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, get your ugly \Nface off of her!
Dialogue: 0,01:10:33.14,01:10:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Look what I got.
Dialogue: 0,01:10:51.79,01:10:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- You all right? \N- Well, I'm not sure.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:05.51,01:11:09.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, according to legend, the black \Nbook the Americans found at Hamunaptra
Dialogue: 0,01:11:09.60,01:11:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,is supposed to bring \Npeople back from the dead.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:11.72,01:11:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Until now, it was a notion I \Nwas unwilling to believe.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:13.85,01:11:16.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Believe it, sister. That's what \Nbrought our buddy back to life?
Dialogue: 0,01:11:16.48,01:11:19.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. I'm thinking that if the black \Nbook can bring dead people to life...
Dialogue: 0,01:11:19.94,01:11:23.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- Then maybe the gold book can \Nkill him. - That's the myth.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:23.70,01:11:26.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, we just have to find out \Nwhere the gold book is hidden.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:26.66,01:11:28.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:28.66,01:11:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:30.45,01:11:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:32.50,01:11:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:34.75,01:11:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:36.83,01:11:40.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:41.17,01:11:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:47.55,01:11:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:49.80,01:11:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:51.10,01:11:55.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Last but not least, my favorite \Nplague, boils and sores.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:55.18,01:11:57.19,Default,,0,0,0,,They have become his slaves.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:57.56,01:12:00.86,Default,,0,0,0,,So it has begun, the \Nbeginning of the end.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:00.94,01:12:03.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Not quite yet, it hasn't. \NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:04.65,01:12:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:06.86,01:12:08.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:08.82,01:12:10.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:13.37,01:12:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:17.75,01:12:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:26.38,01:12:29.22,Default,,0,0,0,,According to Bembridge scholars, \Nthe Golden Book of Amun-Ra
Dialogue: 0,01:12:29.30,01:12:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,is located inside the \Nstatue of Anubis.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:31.39,01:12:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's where we found the \Nblack book. - Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:33.47,01:12:35.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like the old boys at \NBembridge were mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:35.43,01:12:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,They mixed the books up.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:37.14,01:12:38.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Mixed up where they were buried.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:39.02,01:12:42.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So, if the black book is \Ninside the statue of Anubis,
Dialogue: 0,01:12:42.15,01:12:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,then the Golden book \Nmust be inside...
Dialogue: 0,01:12:48.57,01:12:51.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- I think I'll go and get the \Ncar started. - I've got it.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:52.08,01:12:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The Golden Book of Amun-Ra is at \NHamunaptra inside the statue of Horus.
Dialogue: 0,01:13:05.42,01:13:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:13:08.22,01:13:10.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:13:10.97,01:13:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:13:15.97,01:13:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:13:24.98,01:13:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go, let's go, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,01:13:29.20,01:13:31.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Get this thing in gear, boy. \NLet's get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,01:13:31.82,01:13:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- Evy. Come on, Evy. Hurry up. \N- Imhotep!
Dialogue: 0,01:13:34.33,01:13:35.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep!
Dialogue: 0,01:13:42.46,01:13:45.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna get yours, Beni! \NYou hear me?
Dialogue: 0,01:13:45.92,01:13:50.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're gonna get yours! - Oh, \Nlike I've never heard that before!
Dialogue: 0,01:14:20.71,01:14:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang on!
Dialogue: 0,01:14:58.24,01:15:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! O'Connell! O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,01:15:56.47,01:15:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Jump down!
Dialogue: 0,01:16:00.64,01:16:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Move, move, move!
Dialogue: 0,01:16:05.31,01:16:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:07.10,01:16:08.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:09.11,01:16:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:11.15,01:16:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:16.82,01:16:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:21.58,01:16:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the creature.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:23.91,01:16:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,He's fully regenerated.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:31.13,01:16:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Come with me, my Princess.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:33.34,01:16:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It is time to make \Nyou mine forever.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:36.72,01:16:39.01,Default,,0,0,0,,For all eternity, idiot.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:45.14,01:16:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Take my hand, and I will \Nspare your friends.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:49.69,01:16:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, dear.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:53.40,01:16:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- Have you got any bright ideas? \N- I'm thinking, I'm thinking.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:56.19,01:16:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You better think of something fast, \Nbecause if he turns me into a mummy,
Dialogue: 0,01:16:59.70,01:17:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,you're the first one \NI'm coming after.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:06.04,01:17:07.12,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:07.20,01:17:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Don't. \N- No!
Dialogue: 0,01:17:08.33,01:17:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He has to take me to Hamunaptra \Nto perform the ritual.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:10.71,01:17:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,She is right. Live \Ntoday, fight tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:25.85,01:17:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be seeing you again.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:34.69,01:17:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn!
Dialogue: 0,01:17:38.74,01:17:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey, that's mine. \N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:43.32,01:17:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Kill them all!
Dialogue: 0,01:17:44.66,01:17:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Let go of me!
Dialogue: 0,01:17:46.95,01:17:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,- Imhotep. \N- Let go of me!
Dialogue: 0,01:17:48.62,01:17:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- Goodbye, my friend. \N- Come here, you little...
Dialogue: 0,01:17:51.67,01:17:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:17:54.92,01:17:56.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep.
Dialogue: 0,01:18:00.55,01:18:01.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:01.76,01:18:03.76,Default,,0,0,0,,- What about my sister? \N- We're gonna get her back!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:03.76,01:18:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:05.55,01:18:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You're next!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:08.43,01:18:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on! Give me your hand!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:10.43,01:18:12.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- You go! \N- Come on!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:12.69,01:18:13.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:46.64,01:18:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Morning, Winston. A word?
Dialogue: 0,01:18:51.14,01:18:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your little problem got to do \Nwith His Majesty's Royal Air Corps?
Dialogue: 0,01:18:54.98,01:18:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a damn thing.
Dialogue: 0,01:18:58.36,01:19:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is it dasngerous? - You \Nprobably won't live through it.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:00.99,01:19:02.90,Default,,0,0,0,,By Jove, do you really think so?
Dialogue: 0,01:19:02.99,01:19:05.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody else we've bumped \Ninto has died. Why not you?
Dialogue: 0,01:19:05.57,01:19:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the... What's \Nthe challenge, then?
Dialogue: 0,01:19:08.33,01:19:11.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Rescue the damsel in distress, kill \Nthe bad guy, and save the world.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:13.46,01:19:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Winston Havlock at \Nyour service, Sir.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:27.18,01:19:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,01:19:30.06,01:19:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Do I bloody look all right?
Dialogue: 0,01:19:36.56,01:19:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,How you doing?
Dialogue: 0,01:19:47.78,01:19:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,See that? I've never \Nseen one so big.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:52.04,01:19:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- Never? \N- No!
Dialogue: 0,01:20:06.76,01:20:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Get off me! Get off!
Dialogue: 0,01:20:11.64,01:20:13.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I need a new job.
Dialogue: 0,01:20:34.41,01:20:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,01:20:36.41,01:20:37.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We're back.
Dialogue: 0,01:20:50.34,01:20:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell.
Dialogue: 0,01:21:04.48,01:21:06.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,01:21:08.40,01:21:12.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Winston! Pedal faster!
Dialogue: 0,01:21:14.58,01:21:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang on, men!
Dialogue: 0,01:21:59.83,01:22:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop it! You'll kill them!
Dialogue: 0,01:22:02.17,01:22:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the idea.
Dialogue: 0,01:22:19.06,01:22:21.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Here I come, laddies!
Dialogue: 0,01:22:48.84,01:22:52.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I love the whole sand-wall \Ntrick. It was beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,01:22:52.30,01:22:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Bastard.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:11.61,01:23:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah. All right.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:19.12,01:23:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Winston! Hey, Winston!
Dialogue: 0,01:23:36.22,01:23:39.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Quicksand! Get back! \NIt's quicksand?
Dialogue: 0,01:24:53.38,01:24:56.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Bembridge scholars never \Nwrote about this.
Dialogue: 0,01:25:01.26,01:25:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Get off me. Get off!
Dialogue: 0,01:25:49.60,01:25:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Wha... Wha...
Dialogue: 0,01:26:12.83,01:26:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- Can you see... \N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,01:26:14.67,01:26:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- Can you believe... \N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,01:26:17.09,01:26:18.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- Can we just... \N- No.
Dialogue: 0,01:26:29.68,01:26:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who the hell are these guys? \N- Priests.
Dialogue: 0,01:26:33.35,01:26:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Imhotep's priests.
Dialogue: 0,01:26:35.27,01:26:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, then.
Dialogue: 0,01:27:24.74,01:27:26.24,Default,,0,0,0,,There he is!
Dialogue: 0,01:27:27.41,01:27:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello, Horus, old boy.
Dialogue: 0,01:27:38.59,01:27:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to close the door.
Dialogue: 0,01:28:20.79,01:28:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Anck-Su-Namun.
Dialogue: 0,01:28:31.64,01:28:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,01:28:33.85,01:28:35.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Jonathan!
Dialogue: 0,01:28:46.15,01:28:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn. These guys just \Ndon't quit, do they?
Dialogue: 0,01:28:49.20,01:28:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep digging.
Dialogue: 0,01:29:14.56,01:29:16.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The Book of Amun-Ra.
Dialogue: 0,01:29:24.61,01:29:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Save the girl. \NKill the creature.
Dialogue: 0,01:29:45.63,01:29:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You all right. Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,01:30:42.60,01:30:46.36,Default,,0,0,0,,The Book of Amun-Ra! I \Nfound it, Evy! I found it!
Dialogue: 0,01:30:48.15,01:30:51.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut up and get me \Noff here, Jonathan!
Dialogue: 0,01:30:51.36,01:30:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Open the book, Jonathan. It's \Nthe only way to kill him.
Dialogue: 0,01:30:55.03,01:30:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to open the book \Nand find the inscription.
Dialogue: 0,01:30:57.91,01:31:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I can't open it! \NIt's locked or something.
Dialogue: 0,01:31:03.46,01:31:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- We need the key, Evy! \N- It's inside his robes.
Dialogue: 0,01:31:13.68,01:31:14.93,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,01:31:46.79,01:31:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Mummies.
Dialogue: 0,01:31:59.64,01:32:02.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out! There's one there... \NO'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,01:32:28.08,01:32:30.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's an inscription.
Dialogue: 0,01:32:49.23,01:32:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, boy.
Dialogue: 0,01:32:57.82,01:33:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah. This just keeps \Ngetting better and better.
Dialogue: 0,01:33:01.87,01:33:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do something, Jonathan. \N- Me?
Dialogue: 0,01:33:04.12,01:33:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- You can command them. - You \Nhave got to be joking.
Dialogue: 0,01:33:07.16,01:33:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Finish the inscription on the cover, \Nidiot, then you can control them.
Dialogue: 0,01:33:10.75,01:33:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. Right.
Dialogue: 0,01:33:50.25,01:33:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry up, Jonathan!
Dialogue: 0,01:34:23.99,01:34:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- I can't figure out this last \Nsymbol. - What does it look like?
Dialogue: 0,01:34:41.76,01:34:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a bird. A stork!
Dialogue: 0,01:34:58.02,01:34:59.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Ahmenophus.
Dialogue: 0,01:35:01.57,01:35:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, I see.
Dialogue: 0,01:35:49.03,01:35:50.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Anck-Su-Namun!
Dialogue: 0,01:36:01.96,01:36:03.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Anck-Su-Namun!
Dialogue: 0,01:36:31.12,01:36:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Evy, I've got it.
Dialogue: 0,01:36:38.12,01:36:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep him busy.
Dialogue: 0,01:36:43.46,01:36:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,No problem.
Dialogue: 0,01:36:57.35,01:37:00.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hurry, Evy! Hurry! \N- You're not helping.
Dialogue: 0,01:37:09.86,01:37:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! I've got it?
Dialogue: 0,01:37:41.31,01:37:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you said it \Nwas gonna kill him!
Dialogue: 0,01:37:53.58,01:37:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He's mortal.
Dialogue: 0,01:38:30.32,01:38:33.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Death is only the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,01:39:03.56,01:39:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to go.
Dialogue: 0,01:39:15.66,01:39:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You've lost the book! \NJonathan, I can't believe...
Dialogue: 0,01:39:18.58,01:39:20.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hurry! \N- Come on!
Dialogue: 0,01:39:48.56,01:39:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- Couldn't we just... \N- No, Jonathan!
Dialogue: 0,01:39:57.66,01:39:59.16,Default,,0,0,0,,O'Connell!
Dialogue: 0,01:40:01.83,01:40:05.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- O'Connell! Wait! \N- Come on, come on!
Dialogue: 0,01:40:05.29,01:40:08.33,Default,,0,0,0,,- Wait! Please! - Come \Non, come on! Beni!
Dialogue: 0,01:40:10.17,01:40:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye, Beni.
Dialogue: 0,01:40:14.88,01:40:16.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out, look out!
Dialogue: 0,01:41:03.64,01:41:06.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you. Thank you very much?
Dialogue: 0,01:41:06.18,01:41:10.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You have earned the respect and \Ngratitude of me and my people?
Dialogue: 0,01:41:10.10,01:41:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, well, it was nothing?
Dialogue: 0,01:41:12.90,01:41:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,May Allah smile upon you always.
Dialogue: 0,01:41:17.24,01:41:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And yourself.
Dialogue: 0,01:41:25.45,01:41:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes, anytime. - Stay \Nout of trouble.
Dialogue: 0,01:41:29.33,01:41:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,He's just leaving us here?
Dialogue: 0,01:41:36.42,01:41:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I guess we go home \Nempty-handed again.
Dialogue: 0,01:41:40.59,01:41:42.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't say that.
Dialogue: 0,01:41:44.60,01:41:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, please!
Dialogue: 0,01:41:55.73,01:41:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,How about you, darling? Would \Nyou like a little kissy-wissy?
